## The single-profession spec fix

The original spec is explicit: **a provider can only choose ONE profession**, via a
searchable "View All Professions" flow. The old `StepServices` in
`provider_register.jsx` let providers multi-select from a small category grid — that
directly contradicted the spec.

It's now `StepProfession`, built around **`components/service_type_picker.jsx`**: a
grid of common trades (Electrician, Plumber, Cleaner, Painter, AC Technician) with a
final **"View all"** tile — replacing the old fixed "Carpenters" tile — that opens
`components/profession_modal.jsx` (search, categories, icons) for anything not shown.
Single-select only. The same picker is now used in `request.jsx`'s "Service type"
section too, so both flows behave consistently and no longer each keep their own
duplicate hard-coded category list.

## Auth & redirect behavior

`AuthContext` + `App.jsx`'s `Shell` implement the rules from the spec:

- Logged-out users always land on **Login** (via role-selection → "sign in" or directly).
- Logged-in users skip registration and go straight to their dashboard
  (`customer` → CustomerDashboard, `provider` → ProviderDashboard, `admin` → AdminDashboard).
- `mockBackend.auth.onAuthChange` drives this reactively, the same shape a real
  `firebase.auth().onAuthStateChanged` listener would.

