## The mock backend

`lib/mockBackend.js` is a plain in-memory store — no localStorage, no external
dependency, resets on reload. Every function is `async` and returns a `Promise`
so the shape matches what a real Firebase call would look like. When you're ready:

- `auth.register / auth.login / auth.logout / auth.onAuthChange` → Firebase Authentication
- `getFeed / createPost / toggleReaction / addComment` → Firestore `posts`/`comments`
- `toggleFollow` → Firestore `followers` collection
- `getProfessions` → a static `professions` collection (or keep it as a constant — it
  rarely changes)

Swap the internals; the function signatures were written so calling components
(`Feed`, `Login`, `provider_register.jsx`, etc.) shouldn't need to change.

